    "answer": {
      "short": "The number you started with.\n\nBefore crossing out the zeroes, the result is 100 times the starting number.",
      "worked": "Let the starting number be $n$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}(2n+4)\\times5+12&=10n+20+12\\\\(2n+4)\\times5+12&=10n+32\\\\(10n+32)\\times10-320&=100n+320-320\\\\(10n+32)\\times10-320&=100n\\end{align*}$$\n\nMultiplying by 100 appends two zeroes. Since the starting number contains no zeroes, crossing out the zeroes leaves the original number.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
